 ## Production navigation
 
+### Travel to resolved POIs — OD-2026-11-06-A
+
+Dedicated `PRODUCTION-CONTRACTS-POI-RESOLVED-TRAVEL-1`, set 1.16.0, follows the operator's PC playtest so that moving across known ground stays quick. From the map, the company may travel in one committed movement to any resolved POI. RunSystem finds the shortest route over connected, unlocked edges, including authored bypass connections, whose intermediate POIs are resolved or neutralized and are not occupied by a mobile elite; a bypassed optional POI is skipped, never entered or activated. Without such a route this travel is unavailable and ordinary movement remains. The travel counts as one committed map movement: one turn, after which each mobile elite moves at most one edge. A destination occupied by an elite offers the existing Combat or retreat before anything is committed; retreat or front victory leaves the company at its departure POI. For a later rear encounter, the safe return is the route's last POI before the destination when it qualifies as a safe inert return under the Lot E rule; otherwise the threat movement is rejected as Lot E provides. Arrival replays no content and reuses only what a resolved POI already offers, including the services of reusable refuges and of the set 1.15.0 final refuge. The travel adds no saved field: position, visits and turn remain the existing facts. The map pawn follows the route; reduced motion places it directly. Unresolved, locked and neutralized destinations keep their current rules, and every canonical causal gate, exclusive choice and directed recovery link is preserved.
+
 ### Lot E graph encounters — OD-2026-10-15-B
 
 Dedicated `PRODUCTION-CONTRACTS-POI-LOT-E-1`, set 1.4.0, [operator decision and exact authoring](../autonomy/LOT_E_OPERATOR_DECISION_2026-10-15.md): twelve optional fixed POIs extend the existing three-region graph. Two distinct elite actors move on their explicitly authorized local edges only, at most one edge per committed map movement or explicit Wait. Persist their versioned gameplay state; no real-time, physical road, caravan, lane or historical Pursuit simulation is reintroduced. Opening map, focus, pan, activity, save/load and redraw do not tick. Arrival content finishes before the pending turn is evaluated; activation is prerequisite-gated and deferred on an occupied spawn.
